      "content": "To achieve 3NF, you'll need to identify transitive dependencies (also known as analogous dependencies) and split them out into separate tables. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Identify your attributes and their relationships, then look for transitive dependencies (e.g., a department has managers, and a manager has reports, so a department's data should not include manager's data).\n2. Create a functional dependency tree to visualize these relationships, and identify the transitive dependencies.\n3. Normalise each table into 3NF by moving dependent attributes to a new related table.\n4. Ensure that each table has 2NF and follow the process until no further improvements can be made.\n5. Test your 3NF schema by creating backup queries to ensure that no further errors can be caused by leaving ad-hoc data in one place.",
